 record here runs 75 years back to 1951, and October to November came in under 90% of normal in 36 of them on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 55% of normal in October to November and 37% in November to December. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 38% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 18194 had its driest year in 2016 at 54% of normal.</p>"}
